# Valgrind suppressions for Obvious Edit — GLib/GObject internals ONLY.
#
# Scope policy: this file may suppress Memcheck findings whose allocation
# stack lives inside GLib or GObject one-time initialization (the GType
# registry, quark tables, slice allocator, default main context). It must
# never grow entries for project code. Third-party entries are the
# documented exceptions below: one scoped libasound record and one
# scoped libfontconfig record, each for a leak with no upstream free
# path. If a new leak class appears, fix or scope it — do not widen
# this file.
#
# Observed on GLib 2.84.4 / GObject 2.84.4 (Debian 13): ~43 KB of
# "still reachable" blocks allocated by g_realloc inside GObject's static
# type registration during library constructors. These live for the
# process lifetime by design.

{
   gobject-static-type-registration
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: reachable
   fun:*alloc
   fun:g_realloc
   obj:*/libgobject-2.0.so*
   fun:g_type_register_static
   ...
}

{
   gobject-type-init-constructors
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: reachable
   fun:*alloc
   fun:g_*alloc
   obj:*/libgobject-2.0.so*
   ...
}


# GLib's GTask worker thread spawns once per process; its TLS block
# (dl-tls under pthread_create) is reported as "possibly lost" because
# no exported pointer reaches it. GLib-internal one-time allocation —
{
   glib-gtask-worker-thread-tls
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: possible
   fun:calloc
   ...
   fun:pthread_create*
   obj:*/libglib-2.0.so*
}

# libasound's snd_device_name_hint() builds its device-hint list in
# process-global config state and exposes no API to release it; SDL3's
# ALSA backend calls it during audio-subsystem initialization (device
# enumeration at oe_audio_output_init) and intentionally keeps the
# results alive for device hot-plug. One-time per process, upstream-
# owned on both sides of the call. Tests run under SDL_AUDIODRIVER=dummy
# (no ALSA is ever loaded); this entry only matters for valgrind runs
# with a real driver. Scoped to exactly that call path:
{
   libasound-snd-device-name-hint-cached-by-sdl3-enumeration
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: definite,indirect
   fun:*alloc
   ...
   fun:snd_device_name_hint
   ...
   fun:oe_audio_output_init
}

# fontconfig's FcInitLoadConfigAndFonts() builds its configuration and
# font-index caches in process-global state (parsing the system config
# through expat) and exposes no release path; Cairo's toy font API —
# used by the Phase 11 title rasterizer (oe_generator_raster,
# D12/D13) to resolve the pinned 'DejaVu Sans' family — keeps the
# resolved pattern alive for the process lifetime. One-time per
# process, upstream-owned on both sides of the call, and the first
# Cairo font use in the suite triggers it. Scoped to fontconfig's own
# allocations — no project frame can ever match this pattern.
{
   libfontconfig-fcinit-config-caches-via-cairo-toy-font-face
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: definite,indirect
   fun:*alloc
   ...
   obj:*/libfontconfig.so*
}